ort the originally claimed direction, so I reject and close H24. However, the same result indicates an uncertain opposite-direction signal: SMARCA4 loss may have a weaker stronger-dependency association in adenocarcinoma than in its complement. When reversed, the interval would span roughly +0.035 to +0.312, with a point estimate above threshold but a lower bound below threshold, so I do not treat the opposite effect as established. I register a new unresolved reversed-direction proposal linked to H24 for possible follow-up.\n\nThe strict CDKN2A test remains borderline. In cells wildtype for TP53, KEAP1, SMARCA4, and MTAP, CDKN2A loss has a signed estimate of +0.131 (R38; interval +0.065 to +0.196). The point estimate is below the 0.15-unit threshold, although the interval includes threshold-level values. Therefore H49 remains unresolved, and I defer further CDKN2A work unless another strategy can resolve this borderline range. Since SMARCA4 loss is now the strongest accepted main effect without independent validation, I request validation for H4.",
