  "narrative": "I assessed the twelve new discovery results against the pre-specified 0.15-unit threshold, using estimates as signed to each registered direction. The clean-background SMARCA4-by-adenocarcinoma interaction H60/R41 is not threshold-level: signed estimate +0.065 with interval -0.040 to +0.170. The upper bound barely exceeds threshold while the lower bound remains near zero, so this exact refinement does not support established adenocarcinoma-specific attenuation. I close H60 as unresolved. Direct SMARCA4 main effects remain very large in adenocarcinoma: H45/R43 gives +0.760 (0.686 to 0.833), and the cleaner TP53/KEAP1-wildtype adenocarcinoma stratum H61/R42 gives +0.796 (0.743 to 0.848), both with entire intervals far above threshold. These accept H45 and H61 as dataset associations and close those specific subtype main-effect tests. The co-occurring genetic contexts also remain robust and threshold-level: TP53 loss within KEAP1-loss cells H52/R44 +0.878 (0.773 to 0.982), KEAP1 loss within SMARCA4-loss cells H53/R45 +0.790 (0.661 to 0.920), and SMARCA4 loss within TP53-loss cells H54/R46 +0.763 (0.653 to 0.873). I accept and close H52, H53, and H54 as context-robustness checks; they reduce concern that the accepted main associations disappear in one another's presence, but they are not independent replication.\n\nThe most consequential new result is PTEN loss H58/R48. In the claimed stronger-dependency direction, the signed estimate is +0.239 with interval +0.145 to +0.332. Both the point estimate and entire interval exceed 0.15, so I accept H58 in the supplied discovery data. Because PTEN was not among the originally accepted predictors and because its measured co-occurrence with TP53, KEAP1, and SMARCA4 losses could plausibly explain part of the association, I request independent validation for H58 and keep it active. I also register a clean-background PTEN refinement among TP53-, KEAP1-, and SMARCA4-wildtype cells to test whether the PTEN association is independent of the three dominant accepted associations.\n\nThe remaining broad screens do not support meaningful claimed-direction threshold effects. EGFR amplification H57/R47 is borderline in an ambiguous way: signed estimate +0.102 with interval -0.003 to +0.206. The point estimate is below threshold and the interval includes both no effect and threshold-level benefit, so I leave H57 unresolved but defer it rather than allocate additional validation before PTEN is resolved. RB1 loss H59/R49, MYC amplification H63/R50, PIK3CA mutation H64/R51, and ERBB2 amplification H66/R52 all have claimed-direction intervals below threshold, including upper bounds under 0.15, and I reject and close them as not supporting the registered hypotheses. Given the new PTEN signal and the clean-background SMARCA4 interaction result, I defer the remaining full-population SMARCA4-by-adenocarcinoma reversed interaction H51; it remains unresolved, but it is lower priority than establishing whether PTEN is a robust measured predictor and whether it is independent of accepted co-mutation structure. All accepted findings remain associations in this supplied dataset, not causal effects or validated generalizable biomarkers.",
