  "narrative": "All newly returned signed estimates were assessed against the 0.15 absolute composite dependency-score threshold in the claim direction. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is negative, i.e. stronger dependency.\n\nPTEN loss now has a coherent accepted context-restricted association. H145, in the clean TP53-wildtype, KEAP1-wildtype, SMARCA4-wildtype, MSI-stable, MTAP-wildtype background, gives +0.2659 with 95% interval [0.1773, 0.3544]. H146, the same background restricted to adenocarcinoma, gives +0.2911 [0.1856, 0.3966]. Both intervals lie wholly above threshold. I accept these as supplied-dataset associations but only within the stated eligibility contexts; they do not establish a broad marginal PTEN effect or a causal relationship. Because PTEN was examined in many context cuts, the accepted claim should be interpreted as the most defensible clean-context signal, not as confirmation of every PTEN cut.\n\nMSI-high remains exceptionally strong and robust. H147 tests MSI-high within a clean TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4/MTAP/CDKN2A wildtype background and gives +0.7302 [0.6501, 0.8102]. This argues against the association being explained mainly by overlap with those common co-deletion or predictor contexts. The specificity probes further support persistence: MSI-high outside the top mutation-burden quartile, H150, gives +0.8116 [0.6687, 0.9545]; MSI-high in lower aneuploidy, H152, gives +0.7284 [0.5645, 0.8924]; MSI-high among high screen ROC quality, H154, gives +0.7056 [0.5726, 0.8385]; and MSI-high in adherent culture, H155, gives +0.8578 [0.7297, 0.9860]. All far exceed threshold. I accept and close them as supplied-dataset context associations. They reduce concern that MSI-high is merely an artifact of MTAP loss, CDKN2A loss, high mutation burden, high aneuploidy, low screen quality, or nonadherent culture, but they do not exclude other unmeasured dataset structure.\n\nThe modifier tests were largely negative. The mutation-burden interaction for MSI-high, H151, gives signed -0.0666 [-0.2811, 0.1479]. The interval is entirely below the +0.15 threshold and points away from the claimed direction, so I reject the hypothesis that high mutation burden amplifies the stronger-dependency MSI-high contrast. The high-aneuploidy interaction for MSI-high, H153, gives +0.0843 [-0.1364, 0.3050]; this is unresolved, but the point estimate is below threshold and the interval includes both zero and the threshold. I leave it unresolved but closed because it is not a threshold-level modifier. The screen-batch_a interaction for SMARCA4, H160, gives +0.0458 [-0.0957, 0.1872], also unresolved but closed; it does not support a threshold-level batch_a modification, though precision does not exclude all possible modification.\n\nCDKN2A remains unresolved and is not accepted. Within MSI-high, H148 gives +0.0102 [-0.2819, 0.3022] with only 21 exposed observations, so the estimate is too imprecise for a meaningful conclusion. The CDKN2A-by-MTAP-loss interaction among MSI-stable samples, H149, gives signed -0.0363 [-0.2193, 0.1467], below threshold and opposite the claimed direction; I reject this specific interaction. Together with earlier CDKN2A results, these findings do not support reopening arbitrary CDKN2A context cuts.\n\nNo independent validation can be requested because no voluntary validation requests remain. Therefore all conclusions are discovery-level associations in the supplied dataset. I did not assess signature-modifier interactions or PTEN-high-aneuploidy tests because they are currently uninformative relative to the larger number of already tested null modifier lines and multiplicity burden. I deferred them to keep the active ledger clean. Accepted associations remain TP53 loss with weaker dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker dependency, SMARCA4 loss with stronger dependency, MSI-high with very strong dependency, and PTEN loss with stronger dependency in clean genomic contexts. Negative or unsupported findings include constructed marker main effects, most conventional drivers, STK11, MTAP main effect, basic profiling-completeness indicators, most interaction modifiers, and CDKN2A as a threshold-level main effect.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 12 appraise update. No validation requests remain; all results are supplied-dataset discovery associations.\n\nNew accepted context-specific PTEN line: H145 clean TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 wildtype, MSI-stable, MTAP-wildtype PTEN loss stronger dependency +0.266 [0.177,0.354]; H146 same adenocarcinoma-restricted +0.291 [0.186,0.397]. These intervals exceed 0.15 and close the clean PTEN context as a supported association, but not as a broad PTEN main effect.\n\nMSI-high is exceptionally robust and independent of several co-occurring contexts: H147 clean TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4/MTAP/CDKN2A wildtype +0.730 [0.650,0.810]; H150 outside top mutation-burden quartile +0.812 [0.669,0.954]; H152 lower aneuploidy +0.728 [0.564,0.892]; H154 high screen ROC +0.706 [0.573,0.839]; H155 adherent culture +0.858 [0.730,0.986]. All accepted/closed. Modifier tests: H151 mutation-burden high interaction reject +/- -0.067 [-0.281,0.148]; H153 high aneuploidy interaction unresolved closed +0.084 [-0.136,0.305].\n\nCDKN2A remains unresolved. H148 within MSI-high is +0.010 [-0.282,0.302] with only 21 exposed, too imprecise; unresolved closed. H149 CDKN2A-by-MTAP-loss interaction among MSI-stable rejects +0.15 threshold-level interaction: signed -0.036 [-0.219,0.147]. Avoid more arbitrary CDKN2A cuts.\n\nTechnical modifier: H160 SMARCA4-by-screen_batch_a interaction unresolved closed +0.046 [-0.096,0.187]; not a supported threshold-level batch modification. H156-H159 signature-interaction and PTEN-high-aneuploidy tests deferred as low priority/redundant given null modifier evidence and multiplicity.\n\nCurrent supported supplied-dataset associations: TP53 loss weaker dependency; KEAP1 loss weaker dependency; SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency; MSI-high very strong dependency; PTEN loss stronger dependency in clean genomic contexts. Negative/unsupported: constructed markers, most conventional drivers, STK11, MTAP main effect, profiling-completeness main effects, library main e