n association and reducing concern about age confounding. Second, age may modify one effect but not the others; if only one stratum reaches the 0.15 absolute threshold in the accepted direction, the appropriate conclusion would be a supplied-dataset context-specific age association rather than a general age interaction. Third, age-specific estimates may be imprecise because age is missing for some samples and because MSI-high is relatively rare; imprecision alone would not allow acceptance. Fourth, an opposite-direction effect in one stratum would be followed up as a new reversed claim only if it exceeded the 0.15 threshold with interval-level support; otherwise it would remain non-meaningful. I avoid adding more arbitrary context cuts because the broad exploration phase is largely complete and validation budget is exhausted. This step tests a prespecified demographic modifier and should be closed if the interaction and stratified analyses are null, imprecise, or not threshold-supported.",
