  "narrative": "I assessed all newly delivered discovery evidence against the pre-specified 0.15 composite-unit effect-size threshold, using the already-signed estimates. A positive signed estimate supports the registered hypothesis direction; for direction +1 this corresponds to a higher composite score and weaker dependency, while for direction -1 it corresponds to a lower composite score and stronger dependency. No independent validation request is possible because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted.\n\nCDKN2A loss remains the principal unresolved near-threshold predictor. In the fully clean TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4/MTAP/MSI-stable context, high screen_roc_auc H194 gives signed +0.1724 [0.0809, 0.2639], while low screen_roc_auc H195 gives +0.1081 [0.0265, 0.1898]. The high-quality-stratum point estimate exceeds threshold, but the interval lower bound is well below it, and the complementary stratum is below threshold. Therefore neither screen-quality stratum provides interval-level evidence of a scientifically meaningful CDKN2A association. The adenocarcinoma-stratified CDKN2A estimate H22, +0.1530 [0.0670, 0.2391], and the clean adenocarcinoma estimate H62, +0.1509 [0.0721, 0.2297], are also only near-threshold and interval-limited. I keep these unresolved but close the CDKN2A branch because repeated context-specific estimates cluster near threshold without a lower bound above 0.15, and additional arbitrary cuts would raise false-positive risk without a pre-specified validation pathway. H71 tests whether MTAP-positive status modifies the CDKN2A association; R200 gives a near-zero interaction, -0.0193 [-0.2020, 0.1634], with the point estimate actually opposite the claimed direction. I reject MTAP-positive status as a claimed-direction modifier, while noting this does not prove exact zero interaction.\n\nThe co-genomic persistence checks for the main genomic associations are strong. SMARCA4 loss among TP53-intact KEAP1-loss cells H196 has signed +0.8762 [0.7807, 0.9717], and KEAP1 loss among SMARCA4-intact TP53-loss cells H197 has signed +0.8504 [0.7647, 0.9361]. Both intervals lie far above the threshold in the registered direction. I accept these as supplied-dataset context-persistence findings: SMARCA4 loss remains associated with a lower composite score, i.e. stronger dependency, even with KEAP1 loss present, and KEAP1 loss remains associated with a higher composite score, i.e. weaker dependency, even with TP53 loss present. These are mean differences in restricted backgrounds, not causal interaction claims. The reciprocal interaction H32, SMARCA4 loss among KEAP1-loss cells, is near zero: +0.0184 [-0.1238, 0.1607]. Despite an upper bound marginally crossing the threshold, the estimate and interval are centered near zero and provide no credible claimed-direction interaction; I reject it. This is consistent with H33 and supports treating the broad main associations as largely additive rather than modified by reciprocal co-genomic status.\n\nMSI-high persists among TP53-loss cells. H200 gives signed +0.7487 [0.5263, 0.9711], with n=24 exposed and 382 comparator, which satisfies the minimum-cell rule. The interval lower bound is above threshold, so I accept that MSI-high is associated with a lower composite score, i.e. stronger dependency, within TP53-loss eligible cells. The exposed cell is small, so precision is less robust than in larger strata, but the effect is far larger than the uncertainty and is consistent with the broader validated MSI-high finding. This remains an association in the supplied dataset, not evidence of causal dependence or external generalizability.\n\nPTEN-loss boundary checks remain interval-limited. In clean SMARCA4-loss background H198, R197 gives +0.2946 [0.1243, 0.4648]; in clean TP53-loss background H199, R198 gives +0.1975 [0.0330, 0.3619]; and in clean high-aneuploidy context H159, R204 gives +0.2177 [0.1026, 0.3328]. All point estimates are in the stronger-dependency direction and some