  "narrative": "No new independent validation was released and there are no response-deadline claims; assessments_due is empty, and the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. I therefore synthesize the supplied dataset using the pre-specified 0.15 composite-unit threshold. Evidence supports four stable large associations and one moderate context-dependent association: TP53 loss is associated with a higher composite score, i.e. weaker dependency (H13/R1 discovery +0.829 [0.767,0.891]; R26 validation +0.795 [0.709,0.881]); KEAP1 loss is associated with a higher composite score, i.e. weaker dependency (H3/R3 discovery +0.810 [0.745,0.875]; R13 validation +0.738 [0.644,0.831]); SMARCA4 loss is associated with a lower composite score, i.e. stronger dependency (H4/R4 discovery +0.804 [0.742,0.867]; R39 validation +0.827 [0.731,0.924]; H30/R40 clean co-genomic context +0.780 [0.718,0.842]); and MSI-high is associated with a lower composite score, i.e. stronger dependency (H111/R105 discovery +0.775 [0.664,0.885]; R106 validation +0.888 [0.713,1.064]; H200/R199 in TP53-loss background +0.749 [0.526,0.971]). These associations persist across lineage subtype, ploidy, media serum, culture, screen quality, mutation burden, omics availability, age, and several co-genomic backgrounds, and the main claims have independent validation. PTEN loss is supported as a moderate stronger-dependency association, chiefly in genomic-clean or MSI-stable contexts: broad H58/R48 +0.239 [0.145,0.332] with R53 validation +0.195 [0.062,0.328]; H121/R115 +0.260 [0.182,0.338] with R119 validation +0.300 [0.180,0.420]; H133/R130 +0.254 [0.159,0.349] with R132 validation +0.239 [0.108,0.371]; H67/R54 +0.252 [0.169,0.335] with R66 validation +0.263 [0.135,0.392]. The broad PTEN validation interval does not clear threshold at the lower bound, so the correct scientific description is moderate, context-dependent, and less robust than the four main associations. Negative findings: constructed markers D/E