  "research_notes": "Final supplied-dataset conclusions after this appraisal: four large associations remain robust and independently validated overall: TP53 loss associated with higher composite score/weak dependency; KEAP1 loss associated with higher composite score/weak dependency; SMARCA4 loss associated with lower composite score/strong dependency; MSI-high associated with lower composite score/strong dependency. New accepted persistence checks show these main effects remain threshold-supported in STK11-wild-type or SMARCA4-wild-type contexts (H16, H19, H21, H46), adding to previous context persistence but not establishing causality or transportability.\n\nPTEN loss remains a moderate, context-dependent stronger-dependency association, especially in genomic-clean or MSI-stable backgrounds, but its broad effect is less robust than the four large predictors; many specific co-genomic PTEN contexts remain interval-limited. CDKN2A remains unresolved: many estimates are near +0.15 composite units in the stronger-dependency direction, but lower confidence bounds repeatedly fail to clear threshold. EGFR amplification remains unresolved and interval-limited.\n\nDirect media-serum baseline contrasts H201-H203 are rejected as threshold-level associations in the supplied dataset. STK11-by-KEAP1-loss interaction H48 is rejected. IFN-gamma modification of MSI-high H206 is unresolved but closed: point estimate +0.123 is below threshold and lower bound is not supportive, although the upper interval leaves a possible modification. Reciprocal PTEN/CDKN2A co-loss branches H204 and H205 are invalid due insufficient cell sizes and closed without empirical interpretation.\n\nMost other tested predictors and modifiers remain negative or interval-limited: constructed markers D/E/F, research signatures, technical omics availability, CRISPR library covariates, conventional secondary alterations, sex, and most biological or technical modifiers do not provide threshold-level claims. Independent validation budget is exhausted; no further validation can be requested. All conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset only, subject to multiplicity, residual confounding among measured predictors, and uncertainty about biological mechanism or generalizability."
